    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0640" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1950v02/pg624"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.20/8–750</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State for
                        Inter-American Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Miller</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1950-08-07">August 7, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Some time ago you suggested the preparation of an article on inter-American
                    policy similar to the “X” article.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d331-f1"/> Such an
                    article was prepared by Louis Halle, Planning Adviser in ARA, and was published in the July issue of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Foreign Affairs.</hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d331-f2"/> A copy of the
                    magazine is attached and I hope that you will have time to read this excellent
                    restatement of our Latin American policy.</p>
                <p>This policy line has been reflected in three speeches which I have made this
                    year, at the Rotary Club in Charleston, West Virginia last January,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d331-f3"/> at the Philadelphia Bulletin Forum on March 22<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d331-f4"/> and at the meeting of the Pennsylvania Federation
                    of Labor May 9.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d331-f5"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d331-f1" n="1" xml:id="d331-f1-content">
                <p>Documents in file 611.20 indicate that a draft of this article existed at least
                    as early as February 1950.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d331-f2" n="2" xml:id="d331-f2-content">
                <p>“Y,” “On a Certain Impatience with Latin America,” <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Foreign Affairs</hi>, vol. 28, no. 4, (July 1950), pp. 565–579.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d331-f3" n="3" xml:id="d331-f3-content">
                <p>Press Release No. 27, which contains Mr. Miller’s speech of January 11, is
                    included in Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Press Releases</hi>,
                    1950, under date.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d331-f4" n="4" xml:id="d331-f4-content">
                <p>“Inter-American Relations in Perspective,” Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, April 3, 1950, p. 521.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d331-f5" n="5" xml:id="d331-f5-content">
                <p>”The American Way and Standards of Democracy,” <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >ibid.</hi>, May 22, 1950, p. 797.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
